/**
 * Starts a `localization` run after translation instead of a plain auto-dub. Needs `auto_dub`; excludes `onscreen.auto_start`. Lip-sync and on-screen together, when the plan would trim the lip-sync of this media, answer 422 `localization_combination_not_supported`. Its dub stage is the auto-dub: dispatched when translation ends, with the translation context, priced on the processed media duration. A dub stage restarted by resumeJob is a manual dub (`as_written`, speech seconds); `estimateLocalization.details.dub` shows it.
 */
